# EAS copies the whole monorepo working tree, not just tracked files. Without
# this the archive is 4.4 GB, and the upload dies before the build starts:
#   Your project archive is 1.5 GB
#   Failed to upload metadata to EAS Build -> 400 (Bad Request)
#
# 4.31 GB of that 4.4 GB is apps/mobile-bob/.preflight/dd-screenshots — Xcode
# DerivedData from a Preflight screenshot run (libRNReanimated.a alone is
# 279 MB). Excluding .preflight/ takes the archive to ~100 MB.
#
# Patterns must be depth-independent (a bare name, or **/). A rooted path like
# apps/desktop-bob/resources/bin/ silently matches nothing, because eas-cli
# resolves this file relative to the directory holding eas.json, while the
# archive itself is rooted at the monorepo.
#
# Do NOT exclude whole apps/ or packages/ subtrees: pnpm needs all 49 workspace
# package.json files present for a frozen-lockfile install to resolve.

# Reinstalled on the builder
node_modules/

# History
.git/

# Preflight scratch: DerivedData, screenshots, simulator build output
.preflight/
.gstack/

# Native build output — pod install and xcodebuild regenerate these
Pods/
DerivedData/
.cxx/
.gradle/

# Expo / Metro / TS caches
.expo/
.expo-shared/
.cache/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Build output from the other apps in the monorepo (nothing tracked lives here)
.next/
.turbo/
dist/
.output/
.wrangler/
.vercel/
coverage/

# Cross-compiled desktop daemon binaries — unused by a mobile build
bob-darwin-amd64
bob-darwin-arm64

# Local artifacts
screenshots/
.deploy/
*.log
